{"result":"{
  "id": "19045",
  "key": "SFCC-645",
  "summary": "Customer Group Pricing — Cart Price Rule Display",
  "description": "**As a** Shopper, \n\n**I want** my customer group discount to be applied automatically when I log in, \n\n**so that** I see my discounted price in cart and checkout without needing to enter a code.\n\n----\n\nThis story covers PWA display of cart price rule discounts for logged-in customer group members. Cart price rules apply at cart — the discounted price is not visible on PLP or PDP, only in cart and checkout.\n\nAt the line item level, eligible products display Was/Now pricing with an \"X% off applied\" label beneath the item. Items not eligible for the discount (e.g. new season) display at full price with no label.\n\nAt the basket summary level, a discount line shows the promotion name, discount percentage, and discount amount (e.g. \"VIP Preview Summer 26 (20% off) — -$80\"). Unlike promo code discount lines, no Remove action is shown, as the discount is tied to the customer group and not a manually entered code.\n\nThis story uses the test customer group and cart price rule promotion configured in SFCC-38. Configuration of real VIC customer groups and the AP21/Omneo → SFCC customer group sync are not in scope and are Zimmermann's responsibility post-handover.",
  "status": {
    "name": "Code Review",
    "category": "In Progress",
    "color": "yellow"
  },
  "issue_type": {
    "name": "Story"
  },
  "priority": {
    "name": "Medium"
